# Kani runs each wrapper on a real atomic, one thread (src/kani/atomic.rs).
# loom and C11 (the weak-memory half, verus/WEAKMEM.md): every access to a
# counter after it is moved into place goes through these wrappers
# (tests/loom/tests/access.rs: arena.rs names the bound counts and the
# arena count, and policy.rs the position, only in vspec/count.rs calls
# and ghost lines, and moves a count into place raw only where it was
# minted, in `Arenas::put_head` and `put_entry`; api/mod.rs names
# `STATE.word` only in `api::state`, and its two writes are calls of these
# wrappers, `claim_init`'s and `publish_ready`'s; this file mints one
# CountPerm per atomic, in `new`, and no `const` item copies one), so a
# permission's value reads as the last write in its atomic's modification
# order. C++20 orders one atomic's writes in one modification order
# consistent with happens-before ([intro.races]); a read-modify-write
# reads the last value before its own write, for every ordering
# ([atomics.order] p10): `fetch_add`, `fetch_sub`, `swap` and a successful
# `compare_exchange` (the strong form, which fails only when the values
# differ); a load, or a failed `compare_exchange`, reads a write no older
# than the last one that happens before it (coherence), so it returns the
# permission's value at its place in that order. `BoundPred` and
# `FracPred` each name one atomic and ghost state only, so they need no
# ordering across locations, but that an `unbind`'s `fetch_sub` comes
# after the `fetch_add` that minted its ticket: the thread that unbinds
# reads the heap's plain `bound` and `arena`, written when it was bound,
# which a race-free program orders after the binding. `NarenasPred` also
# holds the table entries' permissions and the built arenas, which the
# count's `Release` store and `Acquire` loads publish (a release/acquire
# pair, [atomics.order] p2).
# The count, narenas and position models check these consequences on
# copies of the callers' steps (tests/loom/tests/pins.rs). The GenMC cases
# of tests/genmc/count.rs and narenas.rs run the same wrappers' bodies over
# `core`'s atomics, inside pinned copies of the `Arenas` steps
# (`GENMC_PINS`), with the permissions erased: evidence for the callers'
# hand-offs in those configurations, not for any wrapper's contract
# (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC"). No case runs `Policy`'s own counters (the
# position steps).
# `STATE.word` (verus/WEAKMEM.md, P4) has two writes, `claim_init`'s
# exchange and `publish_ready`'s `READY` store, so its modification order
# is `UNINIT`, `INITIALISING`, `READY`, each written once; the `Release`
# store of `READY` with an `Acquire` load or exchange that reads it orders
# `init`'s plain writes before the reader. The init models
# (tests/loom/src/init.rs) check this on a copy of `init_slow`, `shared`
# and `shared_if_ready` over loom's atomics, not these wrappers (`STATE`,
# `INIT_TID` and `SHARED` are statics built in `const` context, which loom
# cannot construct); the GenMC flags and init cases copy the same steps'
# atomic lines onto `core`'s atomics, pinned to the source in `GENMC_PINS`
# (tests/loom/tests/pins.rs).
fetch_add	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::count_fetch_add, and loom: count::loom_count_bind_assign_unbind and count::loom_count_try_bind_idle_rival, and GenMC: count [rc11 imm arm8] and count_idle_rival [rc11 imm arm8]; not checked: this body under concurrency beyond the part of C11 loom models (stale `Relaxed` and `Acquire` loads within a bounded store history, and no load buffering, as verus/WEAKMEM.md states), which the models run as it is over loom's atomic inside copies of the `Arenas` steps, in the configurations tests/loom/src/count.rs states, and beyond the configurations tests/genmc/count.rs states, which the GenMC cases run it in as it is over `core`'s atomic inside copies of the same steps, each only under the memory models its citation names (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC": no race report under ARMv8, and the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build); a heap's ticket handed to another thread before it unbinds, which no case runs; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the counter's last write, which no GenMC case checks (the cases erase the permissions, `Tracked::assume_new()`, so none sees a ghost value) and tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 571703860, body 3058007043, spec 2982154212
